# Project constitution (adabwana.github.io)

Read the OKF knowledge bundle (`.okf/`) before accepting work — engineering
rules (`.okf/software-engineering/`), workflow (`.okf/workflow/`), and the
bundle index (`.okf/index.md`). The active story, feature, and QA procedure
override generic defaults where explicitly documented.

Work only in the assigned git worktree. Commit before handoff. Use the
file-based handoff helper (`swarm_handoff.sh`) with an exact commit
abbreviation. Do not edit runtime handoff state or send direct tmux messages.

# Project shape

* Language: ClojureScript; single-page app (Reagent, reitit, htmx, Bootstrap).
* Build: shadow-cljs (`npx shadow-cljs release app`); dev `npm run watch`.
* Source: `src/adabwana/` — `data.cljs` (content), `components.cljs`
  (presentation), `pages/` (routes), `routes.cljs`, `core.cljs` (init).
* Deployment: GitHub Pages via `.github/workflows/gh-pages.yml` on `main` push.
* Content source of truth: `~/Documents/projects/resume/resume/atoms/**` plus
  `resume/assemblies/*.yaml`. The site mirrors the selected assembly.
* Generated output: `public/js/` (shadow-cljs build) is disposable and rebuilt
  by CI; `public/resume/*.pdf` are derived artifacts.
* Repo layout: `.okf/` is the reusable knowledge bundle (v0.2); `swarmforge/`
  is project-local orchestration config.

# Boundaries

* `data.cljs` holds plain immutable content — no rendering, no JS interop.
* `components.cljs` / `pages/` render — no business logic.
* Keep host/JS interop out of pure data and out of components where possible.
* Do not commit secrets; keep derived bundles on the `gh-pages` deploy anyway.

# Workflow

* One approved story at a time; use the trimmed chain
  specifier -> coder -> cleaner -> QA.
* The specifier asks questions and obtains user approval before coder handoff.
* Roles forward the exact committed task state downstream; preserve the stable
  task name across the chain.
* The QA terminal broadcast is merge-only. Do not start the next story until
  the current story is complete.
